# pnpm + Corepack in monorepo Docker images

## Why this exists

Root [package.json](package.json) declares `"packageManager": "pnpm@10.28.2"`, but `pnpm deploy --prod` copies only the **filtered** app package into `/app`. If [apps/backend/package.json](apps/backend/package.json) (or [apps/frontend/package.json](apps/frontend/package.json)) has **no** `packageManager` field, the production image’s `/app/package.json` does not pin pnpm.

With `corepack enable` only, Corepack may resolve the **latest** pnpm (e.g. 11.x), which requires a newer Node than Strapi’s Node 20 Alpine image. That produces:

- `ERR_UNKNOWN_BUILTIN_MODULE: node:sqlite` (pnpm 11 on Node 20)

## Rule

- Keep `"packageManager": "pnpm@10.28.2"` (same as root) in **every** workspace package that is deployed standalone (`apps/backend`, `apps/frontend`).
- Backend production runner: after `COPY` from builder, ensure pnpm 10 is available (see [apps/backend/main.Dockerfile](apps/backend/main.Dockerfile): copy Corepack cache from builder + `corepack prepare pnpm@10.28.2 --activate`) so activation does not depend on a second registry fetch when possible.

## Do not

- Do not rely on root `packageManager` alone for `/app` produced by `pnpm deploy` — it is not copied into that artifact.
